<title>PORTUGAL: CMVM lifts suspension of trade in Somague, A.Silva.</title>
<headline>CMVM lifts suspension of trade in Somague, A.Silva.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Financial Markets Committee (CMVM) has lifted a suspension of trade in shares of Portuguese construction groups Somague and A.Silva &amp; Silva effective since Monday, dealers said.  </p>
<p>An announcement in Lisbon bourse bulletin said the two companies were continuing talks over the possible acquisition of A.Silva &amp; Silva's Assiconstroi unit by Somague. &quot;The negotiations continue and it is hoped that the conclusions can be announced soon,&quot; it said.</p>
</text>
